      "verdict": "pass",
      "binding": "RUNTIME TOKEN, not compile-time. DispatchContext's constructor requires a module-private symbol and throws ContextForgeryError otherwise; the only constructing function is handed out once, to the dispatcher module as it loads, and is not on the package surface; state is in an ES private field, so a prototype clone has none. Strength: holds against any in-process code holding only the package (constructor, Reflect.construct, subclassing, prototype cloning, deep import of the compiled module after the peer has loaded). Does NOT hold against code that can rewrite the peer's files on disk or runs under the inspector, and does not stop a body from leaking the genuine context it was handed."
